Pathogenic and non-pathogenic Gram-negative bacteria can produce extracellular vesicles. Fig. 4.2 summarises how two types of extracellular vesicle, OMVs and O-IMVs, are formed.

O-IMVs are formed from the outer membrane and the cell surface membrane. O-IMVs can contain ATP and DNA.
